header financing

// Economics: Principal advances and repayments are excluded from earnings. Claims, waivers,
// write-offs and allocations are internal. Paid profit and company charges are
// earnings; receipt refunds reverse captured cash. Borrower cash paid to outside
// capital or recovery recipients passes through, whether held first or paid direct.

// Terms: loan_kind names the product and caps the term. max_term defaults to
// the longest term the library allows for that kind, and a company may lower it
// but never raise it:
//   mortgage    360 monthly instalments
//   auto         84
//   personal     84 (the default kind)
//   short_term   12 (pay later and other short consumer credit)
// months is the instalment count of one plan. Set it in the program to fix the
// term, or leave it runtime and supply it at create; create refuses a plan
// longer than max_term.

// Pricing is required. amortizing reads profit_rate as an annual rate on the
// declining balance: equal monthly instalments, the last absorbing rounding.
// flat_total reads it as one charge on principal for the whole term (murabaha,
// fixed-fee pay-later). 12,000 at 18% over 12 months costs 13,201.95 amortizing
// and 14,160 flat_total.
// Expose create and sign on installments. A funding composition owns checkout,
// destination funding and returns when disburse_to is funds. The repayment plan
// owns principal, profit, limits and debt cancellation.
// disburse_to: seller pays principal to the seller party at activation (pay later
// with the merchant paid on day one). Capital may refund any paid payment to
// the borrower. Payments stay refundable while the plan is active. The
// payment that clears the last slice completes the plan when no late charge or
// recovery cost is outstanding; otherwise expose complete to close it once they
// are settled or waived. When
// the plan leaves active (paid, written off or cancelled) it sets refundUntil to
// refund_within (default 30d) later, and payment, late charge and recovery cost
// refunds stop at that time. A refund that reopens the plan clears refundUntil, which is set
// from the calculated refundWindow so a restore can clear it. Once it passes,
// nothing can move the plan's payments or late charges, so they stop counting as
// open records. On a return, capital runs unwind: it takes the outstanding
// principal back to capital and cancels open slices with their claims. Seller
// mode debits the seller, who also returns the principal the borrower repaid;
// funds mode needs the hold in return_verified and debits the hold, after which
// the payee's escrow refund returns the down payment and the repaid principal.
// Before delivery, the Product
// operator runs unwind_undelivered on a funds-mode plan whose hold is still
// funded: principal goes back to capital and the hold's unwind_financed returns
// the down payment to the payer and closes the hold as refunded, all in one
// operation, so deliver is refused afterwards. It also cancels proposed and
// assessed late charges and recovery costs: goods that never arrived earn no
// fines. Escrow refund refuses while any plan that is
// not cancelled funds the hold, written off included, so the borrower never
// receives lender principal. A funds-mode plan writes off only once its hold
// has released principal to the seller: principal still held is not a loss, and
// unwind or unwind_undelivered returns it. unwind_undelivered needs no paid
// payments and no collected late charges; refund them first. unwind needs no
// assessed late charges; waive them first. When goods never arrive on a paid plan, the
// Product operator runs unwind_paid once the hold's deliverBy has passed, so an
// early payoff never cuts the seller's delivery window short. It refunds the
// profit of every payment, every share, fine and cost receipt, reverses the
// payoff's profit, fines and costs, cancels the plan, and returns the hold's
// whole price to the borrower; capital keeps the principal the borrower repaid.
// A settlement a lending.distribution has paid out keeps its profit and share,
// since investors hold that profit; only the other settlements' profit is
// refunded. Each refund is its own transfer, so unwind_paid moves the plan to
// unwinding and refunds 64 payments and 16 fine and 16 cost receipts per
// operation; the plan's unwind_step clock runs the next batch a second later
// until none remain, then the plan cancels and the hold refunds. max_history
// (default and most 366) caps the late charges and recovery costs on one plan,
// counted across every late charge attachment. A company lowers it to keep
// payoffs and amendments smaller. If any source account is short, the whole
// action refuses and nothing moves; a company that wants a partial refund
// writes that rule in its own program.
// returned_goods decides the split on returned goods, before or after payoff.
// keep_profit, the default, keeps the profit and fines paid so far with the
// company: unwind runs with payments still paid, and on a paid plan the Product
// operator runs return_hold after the refund window to return a return_verified
// hold's whole balance. refund_all makes unwind wait until capital has refunded
// every payment and collected charge, removes return_hold, and lets unwind_paid
// settle returned goods too.
// Borrower- and seller-directed disbursement exclude collect_down_payment. A down_payment
// there reduces principal but does not collect cash. Price is subject metadata,
// not the borrower limit. The funding composition checks its payer and price.
// Cancelling a plan cancels its debt agreement. Its funding composition owns
// returning any cash collected before activation.
// Approve borrower and portfolio limits before disbursement. Create builds the
// dated slice records from future, strictly increasing dates; disbursement
// refuses once a slice is due. Payments need a separate payment record and pay action.
// Expose parent payoff separately and create a current, unexpired payoff_quote.
// Expose late_charge.create as propose_assessment before the clock can assess;
// provide matching plan, slice and borrower. Fine is fixed money, not a percentage.
// A payment under fines_profit_principal first takes assessed fines and then
// recovery costs, oldest first and at most charge_limit (default 12) of each,
// then profit and principal slice by slice in due order. A payment that would
// leave cash unapplied refuses, so a plan with more open charges than
// charge_limit takes several payments. Collection uses the minimum of payment
// cash and outstanding fine; a partial payment does not settle the remaining
// fine. Recovery cost needs its own record,
// which only the Product operator creates; only it cancels a proposed fine or cost.
// Profit share credits capital's allocatedProfitPayable, not an outside agency.
// Credit lines need adapter binding at activation; draws are ledger advances,
// not evidence of outside funding. Only the line's borrower, the Product operator
// by default, opens and closes the line and creates, draws, repays or cancels an
// advance on it. Only the Product operator creates the portfolio limit and
// approves borrower and portfolio limits. No clock declaration proves retries.

// Cost: the plan holds one principal, unearned profit, earned profit, fine and
// cost claim, so disbursement, payoff, write-off, cancellation and refunds post
// one transfer per party and purpose, whatever the term. Slices, pieces and
// charges are state. Only receipts carry their own transfers: a payment posts at
// most 2 per collected charge, so charge_limit bounds it, and unwind_paid
// batches its refunds. Run hsx cost on the selected policies; every action of a
// 360-month plan stays under one 253-transfer batch. Profit is not a platform
// tariff.

instrument installments(loan_kind: enum(mortgage, auto, personal, short_term) = personal, max_term: integer(1, 360) = 360, months: integer(1, 360) = runtime, max_history: integer(2, 366) = 366, pricing: enum(amortizing, flat_total), profit_rate: percent, charge_limit: integer(1, 24) = 12, disburse_to: enum(funds, borrower, seller) = funds, seller: party?, profit_earned: enum(on_payment, by_schedule, at_disbursement) = on_payment, apply: enum(fines_profit_principal, principal_profit, pro_rata) = fines_profit_principal, payoff_rebate: percent = 100%, write_off_after: duration = 90d, max_extension: duration = 90d, max_amendments: integer(0, 366) = 2, waiver_limit: percent = 100%, amendment_expiry: duration = 7d, payoff_quote_expiry: duration = 1h, refund_within: duration = 30d, returned_goods: enum(keep_profit, refund_all) = keep_profit, allow_overdue: enum(allowed, blocked) = allowed, assessed_fines: enum(carry, require_waiver) = carry, down_payment: percent = 0%, funds: ref?, borrower: party = party(person), capital: party = programOperator, share: percent = 0%, limits: ref<financing.limits> = object(financing.limits), portfolio: ref<financing.portfolio_limit> = object(financing.portfolio_limit)) {
  dependencies {
    funds {
      selector: disburse_to, is: funds
      message: "Attachment `{attachment}` disburses into a hold, but `funds` is not bound."
      fix: "Bind `funds: checkout` to a funding composition. Choose `disburse_to: seller` to pay a seller on activation, or `disburse_to: borrower` only if the borrower should receive the money directly."
    }
    seller {
      selector: disburse_to, is: seller
      message: "Attachment `{attachment}` pays a seller, but `seller` is not bound."
      fix: "Bind `seller: merchant` to the declared business that receives the principal."
    }
  }
  ceilings { max_term { by: loan_kind, mortgage: 360, auto: 84, personal: 84, short_term: 12 } }
  constraints { months: at_most(max_term) }
  revisioned: true
  familyRevision: 1
  summary: "Funding, profit recognition and payment order chosen by the program."
  fields {
    funds: ref<funds>?, borrower: account of borrower, settlementIdentity: text, borrowerLimit: ref<limits>, portfolioLimit: ref<portfolio>
    months: integer = months, maxTerm: integer = max_term, dates: list(date, max_term), historyLimit: integer = max_history
    allocatedPayable: account(capital, cash, "allocatedProfitPayable"), capital: account(capital, cash, "capital"), profitIncome: account(capital, cash, "profitIncome"), loss: account(capital, claim, "loss")
    principalReceivable: account(self, claim), profitReceivable: account(self, claim), profitEarned: account(self, claim), fineReceivable: account(self, claim), costReceivable: account(self, claim), debt: account(borrower, claim, contra, "debt")
    principalOutstanding: money?, principalRepaid: money?, principalReturned: money?, profitReturned: money?, lossRecorded: money?, refundWindow: date?, refundUntil: date?
    scheduledPrincipal: money?, scheduledProfit: money?, payoffRebate: money?, payoffProfitTotal: money?, payoffProfit: money?, payoffReceipt: text?
    unwindAt: date?, paymentsLeft: integer?, finesLeft: integer?, costsLeft: integer?
    openSlices: integer?, openCharges: money?, openCosts: money?, payoffRefunds: integer?
    price: money = subject.price
    downPayment: money = rate(self.price, down_payment)
    principal: money = subtract(self.price, self.downPayment)
    flatProfit: money?
  }
  lifecycle { states: [quoted, signed, active, paid, unwinding, written_off, cancelled], initial: quoted }
  invariants count of { instrument: all(financing.installments), reference: "borrowerLimit", anchor: self.borrowerLimit, states: [active], limit: 366 } <= self.borrowerLimit.activePlans
  invariants sum "principalReceivable.balance" of { instrument: all(financing.installments), reference: "borrowerLimit", anchor: self.borrowerLimit, states: [active], limit: 366 } <= self.borrowerLimit.limit
  invariants sum "principalReceivable.balance" of { instrument: all(financing.installments), reference: "portfolioLimit", anchor: self.portfolioLimit, states: [active], limit: 366 } <= self.portfolioLimit.limit
  action create {
    subject { price: money }
    actor: { party: borrower }
    requires self.borrowerLimit.borrower == self.borrower
    requires self.months <= self.maxTerm
    when pricing is flat_total { calculate: [{ target: flatProfit, op: rate, base: { field: self.principal }, bps: { literal: profit_rate }, rounding: floor }] }
    when disburse_to is funds { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: check, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
    invoke: [{ range: { count: { field: self.months }, maximum: max_term, bind: position }, instrument: slice, action: create, input: { plan: { field: self.id }, borrowerLimit: { field: self.borrowerLimit }, portfolioLimit: { field: self.portfolioLimit }, position: { field: position } } }, { selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [draft], limit: max_term, where: { first: { literal: 0 } } }, action: check_order, input: {} }]
  }
  action sign {
    from: quoted, to: signed, actor: { party: borrower }, input { signedOffer: text, affordabilityReference: text }
    requires count of { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [draft], limit: max_term } == self.months
  }
  action collect_down_payment { allowZero: true,
    from: signed, to: signed, actor: { party: borrower }
    when disburse_to is borrower { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is seller { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is funds { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: collect, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
  }
  action disburse { allowZero: true,
    from: signed, to: active, actor: { party: capital }
    requires self.borrowerLimit in [approved]
    requires self.portfolioLimit in [approved]
    calculate: [
      { target: scheduledPrincipal, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [draft], limit: max_term }, measure: { sum: "principal" } }
      { target: scheduledProfit, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [draft], limit: max_term }, measure: { sum: "profit" } }
    ]
    when disburse_to is funds { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: disburse, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
    when disburse_to is borrower { moves self.principal from self.capital to self.borrower economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: capital } }
    when disburse_to is seller { moves self.principal from self.capital to seller economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: capital } }
    moves self.scheduledPrincipal from self.debt to self.principalReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
    moves self.scheduledProfit from self.debt to self.profitReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
    when profit_earned is at_disbursement { moves self.scheduledProfit from self.profitReceivable to self.profitEarned economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator } }
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [draft], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: activate, input: {} }]
  }
  action complete {
    from: active, to: paid
    calculate: [{ target: refundWindow, op: shift, date: { field: self.now }, milliseconds: { literal: refund_within }, direction: after }]
    set: { refundUntil: { field: self.refundWindow } }
    requires count of { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term } == 0
    requires self.fineReceivable.balance == "0"
    requires self.costReceivable.balance == "0"
  }
  action restore { from: [active, paid], to: active, actor: { parent: payment }, input { refundUntil: date? }, set: { refundUntil: { field: input.refundUntil } } }
  action payoff { allowZero: true,
    from: active, to: paid, actor: { party: borrower }
    input { quote: ref<payoff_quote> }
    requires input.quote.plan == self.id; requires input.quote.revision == self.productRevision
    deadline: { at: input.quote.expiresAt }
    calculate: [
      { target: principalReturned, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principalReceivable.balance }] }
      { target: payoffRebate, op: rate, base: { field: self.profitReceivable.balance }, bps: { literal: payoff_rebate }, rounding: floor }
      { target: payoffProfitTotal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profitReceivable.balance }, { field: self.profitEarned.balance }] }
      { target: payoffProfit, op: subtract, base: { field: self.payoffProfitTotal }, subtract: [{ field: self.payoffRebate }] }
      { target: refundWindow, op: shift, date: { field: self.now }, milliseconds: { literal: refund_within }, direction: after }
    ]
    set: { refundUntil: { field: self.refundWindow } }
    moves self.principalReturned from self.borrower to self.capital economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: borrower }
    moves self.payoffProfit from self.borrower to self.profitIncome capture "payoffReceipt" economics { recipient: capital, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: borrower }, participant: { purpose: pass_through, sourceParty: borrower } }
    moves self.principalReturned from self.principalReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitReceivable.balance from self.profitReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitEarned.balance from self.profitEarned to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    // Each attachment's oldest open charge settles that attachment's charges in
    // one cash transfer; four attachments per kind are enough for any program
    // and settle_payoff refuses if a charge is still open.
    invoke: [
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true, order: [overdueAt] }, action: payoff, input: {} }
    ]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: payoff, input: { identity: { field: self.settlementIdentity } } }, { reference: self.id, action: settle_payoff, input: {} }]
  }
  action settle_payoff {
    from: paid, to: paid, actor: { parent: current() }
    requires self.fineReceivable.balance == "0"
    requires self.costReceivable.balance == "0"
    invoke: [{ instrument: settlement, action: create, input: { plan: { field: self.id }, identity: { field: self.settlementIdentity }, principal: { field: self.principalReturned }, profit: { field: self.payoffProfit }, loss: { literal: "0" }, kind: { literal: "cash" } } }]
  }
  action write_off { allowZero: true,
    from: active, to: written_off, actor: { parent: write_off_request }
    input { overdueSlice: ref<slice> }
    calculate: [{ target: lossRecorded, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principalReceivable.balance }] }, { target: refundWindow, op: shift, date: { field: self.now }, milliseconds: { literal: refund_within }, direction: after }]
    set: { refundUntil: { field: self.refundWindow } }
    due: { at: input.overdueSlice.lossEligibleAt }
    requires input.overdueSlice.plan == self.id; requires input.overdueSlice.openPrincipal > "0"
    moves self.lossRecorded from self.principalReceivable to self.loss economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitReceivable.balance from self.profitReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitEarned.balance from self.profitEarned to self.loss economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    when disburse_to is funds { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: write_off, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: write_off, input: {} }, { instrument: settlement, action: create, input: { plan: { field: self.id }, identity: { field: self.settlementIdentity }, principal: { literal: "0" }, profit: { literal: "0" }, loss: { field: self.lossRecorded }, kind: { literal: "loss" } } }]
  }
  action record_payment {
    from: active, to: active, actor: { parent: payment }
    input { identity: text, principal: money, profit: money }
    calculate: [
      { target: openSlices, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term }, measure: count }
      { target: openCharges, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.fineReceivable.balance }] }
      { target: openCosts, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.costReceivable.balance }] }
    ]
    invoke: [{ instrument: settlement, action: create, input: { plan: { field: self.id }, identity: { field: input.identity }, principal: { field: input.principal }, profit: { field: input.profit }, loss: { literal: "0" }, kind: { literal: "cash" } } }]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "borrowerLimit", anchor: self.borrowerLimit, states: [active], limit: 1, where: { id: { field: self.id }, openSlices: { literal: 0 }, openCharges: { literal: "0" }, openCosts: { literal: "0" } } }, action: complete, input: {} }]
  }
  action cancel { from: quoted, to: cancelled }
  action void { from: signed, to: cancelled, actor: { party: borrower } }
  action unwind { allowZero: true,
    from: active, to: cancelled, actor: { party: capital }
    calculate: [
      { target: refundWindow, op: shift, date: { field: self.now }, milliseconds: { literal: refund_within }, direction: after }
      { target: principalOutstanding, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principalReceivable.balance }] }
      { target: principalRepaid, op: subtract, base: { field: self.principal }, subtract: [{ field: self.principalOutstanding }] }
    ]
    set: { refundUntil: { field: self.refundWindow } }
    when disburse_to is borrower { requires true == false }
    when returned_goods is refund_all {
      requires count of { instrument: payment, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
      requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [collected], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
      requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [collected], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
    }
    requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
    requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [assessed], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
    when disburse_to is funds { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: refund, input: { plan: { field: self.id }, principal: { field: self.principalOutstanding } } }] }
    when disburse_to is seller {
      moves self.principalOutstanding from seller to self.capital economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: seller }
      moves self.principalRepaid from seller to self.borrower economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: seller }
    }
    moves self.principalOutstanding from self.principalReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitReceivable.balance from self.profitReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitEarned.balance from self.profitEarned to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: cancel, input: {} }]
  }
  action unwind_undelivered { allowZero: true,
    from: active, to: cancelled, actor: { party: programOperator }
    calculate: [{ target: refundWindow, op: shift, date: { field: self.now }, milliseconds: { literal: refund_within }, direction: after }]
    set: { refundUntil: { field: self.refundWindow } }
    when disburse_to is borrower { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is seller { requires true == false }
    requires count of { instrument: payment, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
    requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [collected], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
    requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [collected], limit: 1, batch: true } == 0
    moves self.principalReceivable.balance from self.principalReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitReceivable.balance from self.profitReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitEarned.balance from self.profitEarned to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.fineReceivable.balance from self.fineReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.costReceivable.balance from self.costReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: cancel, input: {} }]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [proposed, assessed], limit: 366 }, action: cancel_undelivered, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [proposed, assessed], limit: 366 }, action: cancel_undelivered, input: {} }]
    when disburse_to is funds { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: cancel_undelivered, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
  }
  action return_hold {
    from: paid, to: paid, actor: { party: programOperator }
    requires self.refundUntil < self.now
    when disburse_to is borrower { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is seller { requires true == false }
    when returned_goods is refund_all { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is funds {
      invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: return_paid, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }]
    }
  }
  action unwind_paid {
    from: paid, to: unwinding, actor: { party: programOperator }
    when disburse_to is borrower { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is seller { requires true == false }
    when disburse_to is funds {
      requires self.funds.funds.deliverBy < self.now
      when returned_goods is keep_profit { requires self.funds.funds in [funded] }
      when returned_goods is refund_all { requires self.funds.funds in [funded, return_verified] }
    }
    invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: unwind_batch, input: {} }]
  }
  action unwind_step {
    from: unwinding, to: unwinding, actor: clock, due: { at: self.unwindAt }
    invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: unwind_batch, input: {} }]
  }
  // One batch stays under one 253-transfer operation: 64 payments at two
  // transfers, 16 fine and 16 cost receipts at one, and the closing transfers.
  action unwind_batch {
    from: unwinding, to: unwinding, actor: { parent: current() }
    calculate: [{ target: unwindAt, op: shift, date: { field: self.now }, milliseconds: { literal: 1s }, direction: after }]
    invoke: [
      { selection: { instrument: payment, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 64, batch: true }, action: unwind_paid, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.receipt), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 16, batch: true }, action: unwind, input: {} }
      { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost.receipt), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 16, batch: true }, action: unwind, input: {} }
      { reference: self.id, action: unwind_check, input: {} }
    ]
  }
  action unwind_check {
    from: unwinding, to: unwinding, actor: { parent: current() }
    calculate: [
      { target: paymentsLeft, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: payment, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 1, batch: true }, measure: count }
      { target: finesLeft, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.receipt), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 1, batch: true }, measure: count }
      { target: costsLeft, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost.receipt), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: 1, batch: true }, measure: count }
    ]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "borrowerLimit", anchor: self.borrowerLimit, states: [unwinding], limit: 1, where: { id: { field: self.id }, paymentsLeft: { literal: 0 }, finesLeft: { literal: 0 }, costsLeft: { literal: 0 } } }, action: finish_unwind, input: {} }]
  }
  action finish_unwind { allowZero: true,
    from: unwinding, to: cancelled, actor: { parent: current() }
    calculate: [{ target: payoffRefunds, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: settlement, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [recorded], limit: 1, where: { identity: { field: self.settlementIdentity } } }, measure: count }]
    moves self.principalReceivable.balance from self.principalReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitReceivable.balance from self.profitReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.profitEarned.balance from self.profitEarned to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.fineReceivable.balance from self.fineReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    moves self.costReceivable.balance from self.costReceivable to self.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: settlement, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [recorded], limit: 1, where: { identity: { field: self.settlementIdentity } } }, action: unwind, input: {} }, { reference: self.id, action: unwind_payoff_profit, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.payoffRefunds }, operator: "==", right: { literal: 1 } }, input: {} }]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [collected], limit: 4, where: { payoffLed: { literal: 1 } } }, action: unwind_payoff, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [collected], limit: 4, where: { payoffLed: { literal: 1 } } }, action: unwind_payoff, input: {} }]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [pending, due, paid], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: cancel, input: {} }]
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [proposed, assessed, collected], limit: 366 }, action: cancel_undelivered, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.id, states: [proposed, assessed, collected], limit: 366 }, action: cancel_undelivered, input: {} }]
    when disburse_to is funds {
      when returned_goods is keep_profit { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: unwind_paid_undelivered, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
      when returned_goods is refund_all { invoke: [{ reference: self.funds, action: unwind_paid, input: { plan: { field: self.id } } }] }
    }
  }
  action unwind_payoff_profit { allowZero: true,
    from: cancelled, to: cancelled, actor: { parent: current() }
    moves self.payoffProfit from self.profitIncome to self.borrower economics { recipient: capital, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: capital, reversalOf: self.payoffReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
  }
  records {
    write_off_request: {
      fields { plan: ref<parent>, overdueSlice: ref<slice> }
      lifecycle { states: [requested, applied, cancelled], initial: requested }
      action create { requires self.overdueSlice.plan == self.plan; requires self.plan in [active] }
      action apply {
        from: requested, to: applied, actor: { party: capital }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.plan, action: write_off, input: { overdueSlice: { field: self.overdueSlice } } }]
      }
      action cancel { from: requested, to: cancelled }
    }
    payoff_quote: {
      fields {
        plan: ref<parent>, revision: text?, effectiveAt: date?, expiresAt: date = after(self.createdAt, payoff_quote_expiry)
        principal: money?, earnedProfit: money?, unearnedProfit: money?, rebate: money?, fines: money?, costs: money?, gross: money?, amount: money?
      }
      lifecycle { states: [quoted], initial: quoted }
      action create {
        requires self.plan in [active]
        set: { revision: { field: self.productRevision }, effectiveAt: { field: self.now } }
        calculate: [
          { target: principal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.principalReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitEarned.balance }] }
          { target: unearnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: rebate, op: rate, base: { field: self.unearnedProfit }, bps: { literal: payoff_rebate }, rounding: floor }
          { target: fines, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.fineReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: costs, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.costReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: gross, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principal }, { field: self.earnedProfit }, { field: self.unearnedProfit }, { field: self.fines }, { field: self.costs }] }
          { target: amount, op: subtract, base: { field: self.gross }, subtract: [{ field: self.rebate }] }
        ]
      }
    }
    amendment: {
      fields {
        plan: ref<parent>, dates: list(date, max_term), agreement: text, waiverPercent: percent, waiverEvidence: text, maximumWaiver: percent = waiver_limit
        revision: text?, acceptedAt: date?, staleReason: text?, expiresAt: date = after(self.createdAt, amendment_expiry)
        fineDisposition: enum(carry, require_waiver) = assessed_fines, addedProfit: money = 0 SAR
        principalSnapshot: money?, earnedProfitSnapshot: money?, unearnedProfitSnapshot: money?, finesSnapshot: money?, costsSnapshot: money?
        finesWaived: money?, costsWaived: money?
        extension: duration = max_extension, maximum: integer = max_amendments
      }
      lifecycle { states: [proposed, applied, declined, withdrawn, expired, superseded], initial: proposed }
      action create {
        actor: { party: capital }
        requires self.plan in [active]; requires self.waiverPercent <= self.maximumWaiver
        set: { revision: { field: self.productRevision } }
        calculate: [
          { target: principalSnapshot, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.principalReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: earnedProfitSnapshot, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitEarned.balance }] }
          { target: unearnedProfitSnapshot, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: finesSnapshot, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.fineReceivable.balance }] }
          { target: costsSnapshot, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.costReceivable.balance }] }
        ]
        requires count of { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [applied], limit: 366 } < self.maximum
        invoke: [{ range: { count: { field: self.plan.months }, maximum: max_term, bind: position }, instrument: proposed_date, action: create, input: { amendment: { field: self.id }, position: { field: position } } }, { selection: { instrument: proposed_date, reference: "amendment", anchor: self.id, states: [recorded], limit: max_term, where: { first: { literal: 0 } } }, action: check_order, input: {} }]
      }
      action accept {
        from: proposed, to: applied, actor: { party: borrower }, deadline: { at: self.expiresAt }
        requires self.plan in [active]; requires self.revision == self.productRevision
        requires count of { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [applied], limit: 366 } < self.maximum
        set: { acceptedAt: { field: self.now } }
        when assessed_fines is require_waiver { requires self.waiverPercent == 10000 }
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed, collected], limit: 366 }, action: waive_for_amendment, input: { amendment: { field: self.id } } }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed, collected], limit: 366 }, action: waive_for_amendment, input: { amendment: { field: self.id } } }, { reference: self.id, action: record_waivers, input: {} }]
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(collections.case), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [opened, assigned], limit: 366 }, action: recall, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [proposed], limit: 366 }, action: cancel_for_amendment, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [proposed], limit: 366 }, action: cancel_for_amendment, input: {} }]
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: amend, input: { amendment: { field: self.id } } }]
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [paid], limit: max_term }, action: verify_fixed_date, input: { amendment: { field: self.id } } }]
      }
      // The waivers are state on each charge; the plan's claims drop once per kind.
      action record_waivers { allowZero: true,
        from: applied, to: applied, actor: { parent: current() }
        calculate: [
          { target: finesWaived, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.waiver), reference: "amendment", anchor: self.id, states: [recorded], limit: 366 }, measure: { sum: "amount" } }
          { target: costsWaived, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost.waiver), reference: "amendment", anchor: self.id, states: [recorded], limit: 366 }, measure: { sum: "amount" } }
        ]
        moves self.finesWaived from self.plan.fineReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
        moves self.costsWaived from self.plan.costReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
      }
      action withdraw { from: proposed, to: withdrawn, actor: { party: capital } }
      action decline { from: proposed, to: declined, actor: { party: borrower } }
      action expire { from: proposed, to: expired, actor: clock, due: { at: self.expiresAt } }
      action supersede { from: proposed, to: superseded, requires self.revision != self.productRevision, set: { staleReason: { literal: "economic_revision_changed" } } }
    }
    proposed_date: {
      fields { amendment: ref<amendment>, position: integer(1, max_term), date: date = at(self.amendment.dates, self.position), first: integer = divide(1, self.position), prior: integer = subtract(self.position, 1), previousPosition: integer = sum(self.prior, self.first), previous: date = at(self.amendment.dates, self.previousPosition) }
      lifecycle { states: [recorded], initial: recorded }
      action create { actor: { parent: amendment }, input { amendment: ref<amendment>, position: integer(1, max_term) }, requires self.date >= self.previous }
      action check_order { from: recorded, to: recorded, actor: { parent: amendment }, requires self.date > self.previous }
    }
    date_change: {
      fields { amendment: ref<amendment>, slice: ref<slice>, oldDate: date, newDate: date }
      lifecycle { states: [recorded], initial: recorded }
      action create { actor: { parent: slice }, input { amendment: ref<amendment>, slice: ref<slice>, oldDate: date, newDate: date }, requires unique "amended_slice" on [self.amendment, self.slice] }
    }
    settlement: {
      fields { plan: ref<parent>, identity: text, principal: money, profit: money, loss: money, kind: enum(cash, loss), share: money?, retainedProfit: money?
        allocatedPayable: account(capital, cash, "allocatedProfitPayable"), capital: account(capital, cash, "capital"), profitIncome: account(capital, cash, "profitIncome"), lossAccount: account(capital, claim, "loss") }
      lifecycle { states: [recorded, distributed, refunded], initial: recorded }
      action create { allowZero: true,
        actor: { parent: parent }
        input { plan: ref<parent>, identity: text, principal: money, profit: money, loss: money, kind: enum(cash, loss) }
        requires unique "settlement_identity" on [self.plan, self.identity]
        calculate: [{ target: "share", op: "rate", base: { field: self.profit }, bps: { literal: share }, rounding: "floor" }, { target: retainedProfit, op: "subtract", base: { field: self.profit }, subtract: [{ field: self.share }] }]
        moves self.share from self.profitIncome to self.allocatedPayable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: capital }
      }
      action refund { allowZero: true,
        from: recorded, to: refunded, actor: { parent: payment }
        moves self.share from self.allocatedPayable to self.profitIncome economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: capital }
      }
      action distribute { from: recorded, to: distributed, actor: { parent: all(lending.distribution) } }
      // profitIncome is one account per capital party, so refunding profit a
      // distribution already paid out would spend other plans' profit. unwind_paid
      // unwinds only settlements still recorded, and each payment refunds its
      // profit only when its settlement was one of them.
      action unwind { allowZero: true,
        from: recorded, to: refunded, actor: { parent: [parent, payment] }
        moves self.share from self.allocatedPayable to self.profitIncome economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: capital }
      }
    }
    slice: {
      revisioned: true
      fields {
        plan: ref<parent>, borrowerLimit: ref<limits>, portfolioLimit: ref<portfolio>, position: integer(1, max_term)
        originalDueAt: date = at(self.plan.dates, self.position), dueAt: date?, nextDueAt: date?, previousDueAt: date?, prior: integer = subtract(self.position, 1), previousPosition: integer = sum(self.prior, self.first), previousDate: date = at(self.plan.dates, self.previousPosition), extensionLimit: date = after(self.originalDueAt, max_extension), lossEligibleAt: date?
        first: integer = divide(1, self.position)
        principalBase: money?, principalAllocated: money?, principalRemainder: money?, principalAdjustment: money?
        profitBase: money?, profitAllocated: money?, profitRemainder: money?, profitAdjustment: money?
        principal: money, profit: money, instalment: money
        openPrincipal: money?, openProfit: money?, earnedProfit: money?, payoffIdentity: text?
        collectibleProfit: money?, collectibleTotal: money?, paymentBudget: money?, principalRatio: money?, principalBasePayment: money?, profitBudget: money?
        principalTake: money?, profitTake: money?, afterTake: money?, openProfitTake: money?, earnedProfitTake: money?, taken: money?
        ratioDenominator: integer = sum(10000, profit_rate)
      }
      lifecycle { states: [draft, pending, due, paid, written_off, cancelled], initial: draft }
      action create {
        actor: { parent: parent }
        input { plan: ref<parent>, borrowerLimit: ref<limits>, portfolioLimit: ref<portfolio>, position: integer(1, max_term) }
        set: { dueAt: { field: self.originalDueAt } }
        calculate: [
          { target: openPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }
          { target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }
          { target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }
        ]
        when pricing is flat_total {
          calculate: [
            { target: principalBase, op: divide, amount: { field: self.plan.principal }, divisor: { field: self.plan.months }, rounding: floor }
            { target: principalAllocated, op: multiply, amount: { field: self.principalBase }, units: { field: self.plan.months } }
            { target: principalRemainder, op: subtract, base: { field: self.plan.principal }, subtract: [{ field: self.principalAllocated }] }
            { target: principalAdjustment, op: multiply, amount: { field: self.principalRemainder }, units: { field: self.first } }
            { target: principal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principalBase }, { field: self.principalAdjustment }] }
            { target: profitBase, op: divide, amount: { field: self.plan.flatProfit }, divisor: { field: self.plan.months }, rounding: floor }
            { target: profitAllocated, op: multiply, amount: { field: self.profitBase }, units: { field: self.plan.months } }
            { target: profitRemainder, op: subtract, base: { field: self.plan.flatProfit }, subtract: [{ field: self.profitAllocated }] }
            { target: profitAdjustment, op: multiply, amount: { field: self.profitRemainder }, units: { field: self.first } }
            { target: profit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profitBase }, { field: self.profitAdjustment }] }
            { target: instalment, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principal }, { field: self.profit }] }
          ]
        }
        when pricing is amortizing {
          calculate: [
            { target: principal, op: annuity, amount: { field: self.plan.principal }, rate: { literal: profit_rate }, periods: { field: self.plan.months }, position: { field: self.position }, part: principal }
            { target: profit, op: annuity, amount: { field: self.plan.principal }, rate: { literal: profit_rate }, periods: { field: self.plan.months }, position: { field: self.position }, part: interest }
            { target: instalment, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principal }, { field: self.profit }] }
          ]
        }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: refresh_loss_date, input: {} }]
        requires self.plan in [quoted]; requires unique "signed_position" on [self.plan, self.position]; requires self.borrowerLimit == self.plan.borrowerLimit; requires self.portfolioLimit == self.plan.portfolioLimit
        requires self.originalDueAt > self.now; requires self.originalDueAt >= self.previousDate
      }
      action check_order { from: draft, to: draft, actor: { parent: parent }, requires self.originalDueAt > self.previousDate }
      action refresh_loss_date {
        from: [draft, pending, due], to: draft, actor: { parent: current() }
        calculate: [{ target: lossEligibleAt, op: shift, date: { field: self.dueAt }, milliseconds: { literal: write_off_after }, direction: after }]
      }
      action amend {
        from: [pending, due], to: pending, actor: { parent: amendment }, input { amendment: ref<amendment> }
        requires input.amendment.plan == self.plan
        when allow_overdue is blocked { requires self.dueAt > self.now }
        calculate: [
          { target: nextDueAt, op: at, list: input.amendment.dates, position: { field: self.position } }
          { target: lossEligibleAt, op: shift, date: { field: self.nextDueAt }, milliseconds: { literal: write_off_after }, direction: after }
        ]
        requires self.nextDueAt > self.now; requires self.nextDueAt >= self.dueAt; requires self.nextDueAt <= self.extensionLimit
        set: { previousDueAt: { field: self.dueAt }, dueAt: { field: self.nextDueAt } }
        invoke: [{ instrument: date_change, action: create, input: { amendment: { field: input.amendment }, slice: { field: self.id }, oldDate: { field: self.previousDueAt }, newDate: { field: self.nextDueAt } } }]
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: recognition, reference: "slice", anchor: self.id, states: [pending], limit: 1 }, action: reschedule, input: {} }] }
      }
      action verify_fixed_date {
        from: paid, to: paid, actor: { parent: amendment }, input { amendment: ref<amendment> }
        calculate: [{ target: nextDueAt, op: at, list: input.amendment.dates, position: { field: self.position } }]
        requires self.nextDueAt == self.dueAt
      }
      // The plan posts the claims; a slice keeps its share as state.
      action activate {
        from: draft, to: pending, actor: { parent: parent }
        requires self.dueAt > self.now
        calculate: [{ target: openPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principal }] }]
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule {
          calculate: [{ target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profit }] }]
          invoke: [{ instrument: recognition, action: create, input: { slice: { field: self.id } } }]
        }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profit }] }] }
      }
      action mature {
        from: pending, to: due, actor: clock, due: { at: self.dueAt }
      }
      action recognise {
        from: [pending, due, paid, written_off, cancelled], to: preserve, actor: { parent: recognition }
        calculate: [{ target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }, { field: self.openProfit }] }]
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: clear_unearned, input: {} }]
      }
      action clear_unearned {
        from: [pending, due, paid, written_off, cancelled], to: preserve, actor: { parent: current() }
        calculate: [{ target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }]
      }
      action collect {
        from: [pending, due], to: preserve, actor: { parent: payment }
        input { payment: ref<payment> }
        requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.openProfit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }] }] }
        calculate: [
          { target: principalTake, op: minimum, values: [{ field: input.payment.unapplied }, { field: self.openPrincipal }] }
          { target: afterTake, op: subtract, base: { field: input.payment.unapplied }, subtract: [{ field: self.principalTake }] }
          { target: profitTake, op: minimum, values: [{ field: self.afterTake }, { field: self.collectibleProfit }] }
        ]
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: take, input: { payment: { field: input.payment } } }]
      }
      action collect_waterfall {
        from: [pending, due], to: preserve, actor: { parent: payment }, input { payment: ref<payment> }
        requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.openProfit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }] }] }
        calculate: [
          { target: profitTake, op: minimum, values: [{ field: input.payment.unapplied }, { field: self.collectibleProfit }] }
          { target: afterTake, op: subtract, base: { field: input.payment.unapplied }, subtract: [{ field: self.profitTake }] }
          { target: principalTake, op: minimum, values: [{ field: self.afterTake }, { field: self.openPrincipal }] }
        ]
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: take, input: { payment: { field: input.payment } } }]
      }
      action collect_pro_rata {
        from: [pending, due], to: preserve, actor: { parent: payment }, input { payment: ref<payment> }
        requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.openProfit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: collectibleProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }] }] }
        calculate: [
          { target: collectibleTotal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.openPrincipal }, { field: self.collectibleProfit }] }
          { target: paymentBudget, op: minimum, values: [{ field: input.payment.unapplied }, { field: self.collectibleTotal }] }
        ]
        when pricing is flat_total { calculate: [{ target: principalRatio, op: ratio, amount: { field: self.paymentBudget }, numerator: { literal: 10000 }, denominator: { field: self.ratioDenominator }, rounding: floor }] }
        when pricing is amortizing { calculate: [{ target: principalRatio, op: ratio, amount: { field: self.paymentBudget }, numerator: { field: self.principal }, denominator: { field: self.instalment }, rounding: floor }] }
        calculate: [
          { target: principalBasePayment, op: minimum, values: [{ field: self.principalRatio }, { field: self.openPrincipal }] }
          { target: profitBudget, op: subtract, base: { field: self.paymentBudget }, subtract: [{ field: self.principalBasePayment }] }
          { target: profitTake, op: minimum, values: [{ field: self.profitBudget }, { field: self.collectibleProfit }] }
          { target: principalTake, op: subtract, base: { field: self.paymentBudget }, subtract: [{ field: self.profitTake }] }
        ]
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: take, input: { payment: { field: input.payment } } }]
      }
      // A collect action chose principalTake and profitTake; take records them
      // as pieces, lowers the slice's open amounts and the payment's unapplied
      // cash. The payment posts the cash and claim transfers once.
      action take {
        from: [pending, due], to: preserve, actor: { parent: current() }, input { payment: ref<payment> }
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: openProfitTake, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profitTake }] }, { target: earnedProfitTake, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { calculate: [{ target: openProfitTake, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: earnedProfitTake, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profitTake }] }] }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: openProfitTake, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: earnedProfitTake, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.profitTake }] }] }
        calculate: [
          { target: taken, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.principalTake }, { field: self.profitTake }] }
          { target: openPrincipal, op: subtract, base: { field: self.openPrincipal }, subtract: [{ field: self.principalTake }] }
          { target: openProfit, op: subtract, base: { field: self.openProfit }, subtract: [{ field: self.openProfitTake }] }
          { target: earnedProfit, op: subtract, base: { field: self.earnedProfit }, subtract: [{ field: self.earnedProfitTake }] }
        ]
        invoke: [
          { instrument: principal_piece, action: create, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.principalTake }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { plan: { field: self.plan }, slice: { field: self.id }, payment: { field: input.payment }, amount: { field: self.principalTake } } }
          { instrument: profit_piece, action: create, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.profitTake }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { plan: { field: self.plan }, slice: { field: self.id }, payment: { field: input.payment }, amount: { field: self.profitTake } } }
          { reference: input.payment, action: consume, input: { amount: { field: self.taken } } }
          { selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [pending, due], limit: 1, where: { id: { field: self.id }, openPrincipal: { literal: "0" }, openProfit: { literal: "0" }, earnedProfit: { literal: "0" } } }, action: complete, input: {} }
        ]
      }
      action complete {
        from: [pending, due], to: paid
        requires self.openPrincipal == "0"; requires self.openProfit == "0"; requires self.earnedProfit == "0"
      }
      action unpay {
        from: [pending, due, paid], to: pending, actor: { parent: [principal_piece, profit_piece] }
        input { principal: money, profit: money }
        calculate: [{ target: openPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.openPrincipal }, { field: input.principal }] }]
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.openProfit }, { field: input.profit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { calculate: [{ target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }, { field: input.profit }] }] }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.earnedProfit }, { field: input.profit }] }] }
      }
      action payoff {
        from: [pending, due], to: paid, actor: { parent: parent }, input { identity: text }
        set: { payoffIdentity: { field: input.identity } }
        calculate: [{ target: openPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }]
      }
      action write_off {
        from: [pending, due], to: written_off, actor: { parent: parent }
        calculate: [{ target: openPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }]
      }
      action cancel {
        from: [pending, due, paid], to: cancelled, actor: { parent: parent }
        calculate: [{ target: openPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: openProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: earnedProfit, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }]
      }
    }
    recognition: {
      fields { slice: ref<slice>, dueAt: date = after(self.slice.dueAt, 0) }
      lifecycle { states: [pending, recognised], initial: pending }
      action create { actor: { parent: slice }, input { slice: ref<slice> }, requires unique "profit_recognition" on [self.slice] }
      action reschedule { from: pending, to: pending, actor: { parent: slice }, calculate: [{ target: dueAt, op: shift, date: { field: self.slice.dueAt }, milliseconds: { literal: 0 }, direction: after }] }
      action mature { allowZero: true,
        from: pending, to: recognised, actor: clock, due: { at: self.dueAt }
        moves self.slice.openProfit from self.slice.plan.profitReceivable to self.slice.plan.profitEarned economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.slice, action: recognise, input: {} }]
      }
    }
    payment: {
      revisioned: true
      fields { plan: ref<parent>, amount: money, paymentIdentity: text, held: account of self, cashReceipt: text?
        outstandingPrincipal: money?, outstandingProfit: money?, outstandingFines: money?, outstandingCosts: money?, outstandingTotal: money?, unapplied: money?, principalReturned: money?, profitReturned: money?, settled: integer? }

      lifecycle { states: [pending, paid, refunded], initial: pending }
      action create { input { plan: ref<parent>, amount: money, paymentIdentity: text } requires self.plan in [active]; requires unique "payment_identity" on [self.plan, self.paymentIdentity] }
      action pay {
        from: pending, to: paid, actor: { party: borrower }
        calculate: [{ target: outstandingPrincipal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.principalReceivable.balance }] }]
        when profit_earned is on_payment { calculate: [{ target: outstandingProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitReceivable.balance }] }] }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { calculate: [{ target: outstandingProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitEarned.balance }] }] }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { calculate: [{ target: outstandingProfit, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.profitEarned.balance }] }] }
        when apply is fines_profit_principal {
          calculate: [{ target: outstandingFines, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.fineReceivable.balance }] }, { target: outstandingCosts, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.plan.costReceivable.balance }] }, { target: outstandingTotal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.outstandingPrincipal }, { field: self.outstandingProfit }, { field: self.outstandingFines }, { field: self.outstandingCosts }] }]
        }
        when apply is principal_profit { calculate: [{ target: outstandingTotal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.outstandingPrincipal }, { field: self.outstandingProfit }] }] }
        when apply is pro_rata { calculate: [{ target: outstandingTotal, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.outstandingPrincipal }, { field: self.outstandingProfit }] }] }
        requires self.plan in [active]; requires self.amount <= self.outstandingTotal
        moves self.amount from self.plan.borrower to self.held economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: borrower }
        when apply is fines_profit_principal {
          invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: charge_limit, order: [overdueAt] }, action: collect, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.held.balance }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { payment: { field: self.id } } }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: charge_limit, order: [overdueAt] }, action: collect, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.held.balance }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { payment: { field: self.id } } }]
        }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: allocate, input: {} }, { reference: self.id, action: record, input: {} }]
      }
      action allocate {
        from: paid, to: paid, actor: { parent: current() }
        calculate: [{ target: unapplied, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.held.balance }] }]
        when apply is principal_profit {
          invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: collect, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.unapplied }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { payment: { field: self.id } } }]
        }
        when apply is fines_profit_principal {
          invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: collect_waterfall, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.unapplied }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { payment: { field: self.id } } }]
        }
        when apply is pro_rata {
          invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: slice, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [pending, due], limit: max_term, order: [position] }, action: collect_pro_rata, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.unapplied }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { payment: { field: self.id } } }]
        }
      }
      action consume {
        from: paid, to: paid, actor: { parent: slice }, input { amount: money }
        calculate: [{ target: unapplied, op: subtract, base: { field: self.unapplied }, subtract: [{ field: input.amount }] }]
      }
      action record { allowZero: true,
        from: paid, to: paid, actor: { parent: current() }
        requires self.unapplied == "0"
        calculate: [{ target: principalReturned, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: principal_piece, reference: "payment", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: max_term }, measure: { sum: "amount" } }, { target: profitReturned, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: profit_piece, reference: "payment", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: max_term }, measure: { sum: "amount" } }]
        moves self.principalReturned from self.held to self.plan.capital economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: programOperator }
        moves self.profitReturned from self.held to self.plan.profitIncome capture "cashReceipt" economics { recipient: capital, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: borrower }, participant: { purpose: pass_through, sourceParty: programOperator } }
        moves self.principalReturned from self.plan.principalReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
        when profit_earned is on_payment { moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.profitReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator } }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.profitEarned to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator } }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.profitEarned to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator } }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.plan, action: record_payment, input: { identity: { field: self.paymentIdentity }, principal: { field: self.principalReturned }, profit: { field: self.profitReturned } } }]
      }
      // unwind_paid refunds this payment's profit only when its settlement is
      // still recorded; a distributed settlement keeps it with investors.
      action unwind_paid {
        from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: parent }
        calculate: [{ target: settled, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: settlement, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [recorded], limit: 1, where: { identity: { field: self.paymentIdentity } } }, measure: count }]
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: settlement, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [recorded], limit: 1, where: { identity: { field: self.paymentIdentity } } }, action: unwind, input: {} }, { reference: self.id, action: unwind_profit, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.settled }, operator: "==", right: { literal: 1 } }, input: {} }]
      }
      action unwind_profit { allowZero: true,
        from: refunded, to: refunded, actor: { parent: current() }
        moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.profitIncome to self.plan.borrower economics { recipient: capital, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: capital, reversalOf: self.cashReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
      }
      action refund { allowZero: true,
        from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { party: capital }, deadline: { at: self.plan.refundUntil }
        requires unique "settlement_consumption" on [self.plan, self.paymentIdentity]; requires self.plan in [active, paid]
        requires count of { instrument: settlement, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [recorded], limit: 1, where: { identity: { field: self.paymentIdentity } } } == 1
        moves self.principalReturned from self.plan.capital to self.plan.borrower economics { purpose: principal, sourceParty: capital }
        moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.profitIncome to self.plan.borrower economics { recipient: capital, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: capital, reversalOf: self.cashReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
        moves self.principalReturned from self.plan.debt to self.plan.principalReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
        when profit_earned is on_payment { moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.debt to self.plan.profitReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower } }
        when profit_earned is by_schedule { moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.debt to self.plan.profitEarned economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower } }
        when profit_earned is at_disbursement { moves self.profitReturned from self.plan.debt to self.plan.profitEarned economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower } }
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: settlement, reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [recorded], limit: 1, where: { identity: { field: self.paymentIdentity } } }, action: refund, input: {} }]
        when apply is fines_profit_principal {
          invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.receipt), reference: "payment", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: charge_limit }, action: refund, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost.receipt), reference: "payment", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: charge_limit }, action: refund, input: {} }]
        }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.plan, action: restore, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: principal_piece, reference: "payment", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: max_term }, action: refund, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: profit_piece, reference: "payment", anchor: self.id, states: [paid], limit: max_term }, action: refund, input: {} }]
      }
    }
    principal_piece: {
      fields { plan: ref<parent>, slice: ref<slice>, payment: ref<payment>, amount: money }
      lifecycle { states: [paid, refunded], initial: paid }
      action create {
        actor: { parent: slice }
        input { plan: ref<parent>, slice: ref<slice>, payment: ref<payment>, amount: money }
        requires unique "principal_receipt" on [self.slice, self.payment]
      }
      action refund {
        from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: payment }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.slice, action: unpay, input: { principal: { field: self.amount }, profit: { literal: "0" } } }]
      }
    }
    profit_piece: {
      fields { plan: ref<parent>, slice: ref<slice>, payment: ref<payment>, amount: money }
      lifecycle { states: [paid, refunded], initial: paid }
      action create {
        actor: { parent: slice }
        input { plan: ref<parent>, slice: ref<slice>, payment: ref<payment>, amount: money }
        requires unique "profit_receipt" on [self.slice, self.payment]
      }
      action refund {
        from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: payment }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.slice, action: unpay, input: { principal: { literal: "0" }, profit: { field: self.amount } } }]
      }
    }
  }
}

// A late charge and its recovery costs keep their open amount as state. The
// plan's fineReceivable and costReceivable hold the claims, so assessment,
// waiver and refund post one claim transfer each, and payoff and amendment post
// one per attachment or kind, not one per charge.
instrument late_charge(on: ref<financing.installments>[], grace: duration = 3d, fine: money = 50 SAR, cap: money = 25 SAR, fines_to: party = programOperator, costs_to: party = programOperator, borrower: party = party(person)) {
  parameterDiagnostics {
    fine {
      accepts: "a fixed amount"
      percentage: "a percentage of overdue debt"
      fix: "Use a fixed amount only if that is the intended policy. A percentage charge needs an authored rate calculation; do not approximate it with a cash amount."
    }
  }
  revisioned: true
  familyRevision: 1
  summary: "Separate fine and evidenced recovery claims on an overdue installment."
  fields {
    plan: ref<on>, slice: ref<on.slice>, borrower: account of borrower, fine: money = fine, overdueAt: date?, payoffAmount: money?, payoffReceipt: text?, payoffLed: integer?
    open: money?, take: money?
  }
  lifecycle { states: [proposed, assessed, collected, waived], initial: proposed }
  action create { input { slice: ref<on.slice>? }, calculate: [{ target: overdueAt, op: shift, date: { field: self.slice.dueAt }, milliseconds: { literal: grace }, direction: after }, { target: payoffAmount, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: open, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }], requires unique "late_assessment" on [self.slice, self.overdueAt]; requires self.borrower == self.slice.plan.borrower; requires self.plan == self.slice.plan; requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [proposed, assessed, collected], limit: 366 } < self.plan.historyLimit }
  action assess { allowZero: true,
    from: proposed, to: assessed, actor: clock, due: { at: self.overdueAt }
    requires self.slice.openPrincipal > "0"
    calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.fine }] }]
    moves self.fine from self.plan.debt to self.plan.fineReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
  }
  action collect {
    from: [assessed, collected], to: assessed, actor: { parent: child(on, payment) }, input { payment: ref<on.payment> }
    requires input.payment in [paid]
    requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
    calculate: [{ target: take, op: minimum, values: [{ field: input.payment.held.balance }, { field: self.open }] }]
    invoke: [{ instrument: receipt, action: create, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.take }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { plan: { field: self.plan }, assessment: { field: self.id }, payment: { field: input.payment }, amount: { field: self.take } } }, { reference: self.id, action: reduce, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: 1, where: { id: { field: self.id }, open: { literal: "0" } } }, action: finish, input: {} }]
  }
  // The oldest open charge of an attachment settles them all in one transfer.
  action payoff { allowZero: true,
    from: assessed, to: collected, actor: { parent: on }
    requires self.plan in [paid]
    calculate: [{ target: payoffAmount, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: 366 }, measure: { sum: "open" } }]
    set: { payoffLed: { literal: 1 } }
    moves self.payoffAmount from self.plan.borrower to fines_to capture "payoffReceipt" economics { recipient: fines_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: borrower }, participant: { purpose: pass_through, sourceParty: borrower } }
    moves self.payoffAmount from self.plan.fineReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: 366 }, action: close, input: {} }, { reference: self.id, action: close, input: {} }]
  }
  action close { from: [assessed, collected], to: collected, actor: { parent: current() }, calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }] }
  action unwind_payoff { allowZero: true,
    from: collected, to: collected, actor: { parent: on }
    set: { payoffLed: { literal: 2 } }
    moves self.payoffAmount from fines_to to self.plan.borrower economics { recipient: fines_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: fines_to, reversalOf: self.payoffReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
  }
  action finish { from: assessed, to: collected, actor: { parent: current() }, requires self.open == "0" }
  action reduce { from: [assessed, collected, waived], to: preserve, actor: { parent: current() }, calculate: [{ target: open, op: subtract, base: { field: self.open }, subtract: [{ field: self.take }] }] }
  action cancel { from: proposed, to: waived, actor: { party: programOperator } }
  action cancel_for_amendment { from: proposed, to: waived, actor: { parent: child(on, amendment) } }
  action cancel_undelivered { from: [proposed, assessed, collected], to: waived, actor: { parent: on }, calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }] }
  action waive_for_amendment {
    from: [assessed, collected], to: assessed, actor: { parent: child(on, amendment) }, input { amendment: ref<on.amendment> }
    requires input.amendment.plan == self.plan; requires input.amendment in [applied]
    calculate: [{ target: take, op: rate, base: { field: self.open }, bps: { field: input.amendment.waiverPercent }, rounding: floor }]
    invoke: [{ instrument: waiver, action: create, input: { assessment: { field: self.id }, amendment: { field: input.amendment }, amount: { field: self.take } } }, { reference: self.id, action: reduce, input: {} }]
  }
  action waive { allowZero: true,
    from: [assessed, collected], to: waived, actor: { parent: waiver_request }, input { reason: text, evidence: text }
    calculate: [{ target: take, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.open }] }]
    moves self.take from self.plan.fineReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
    invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: reduce, input: {} }]
  }
  action refund {
    from: [assessed, collected], to: preserve, actor: { party: fines_to }, input { payment: ref<on.payment> }, deadline: { at: self.plan.refundUntil }
    requires input.payment in [paid, refunded]
    requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
    invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: receipt, reference: "payment", anchor: input.payment, states: [paid], limit: 1, where: { assessment: { field: self.id } } }, action: refund, input: {} }]
  }
  action reopen {
    from: [assessed, collected], to: assessed, actor: { parent: receipt }, input { amount: money }
    calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.open }, { field: input.amount }] }]
  }
  records {
    waiver_request: {
      fields { assessment: ref<parent>, reason: text, evidence: text }
      lifecycle { states: [requested, applied, cancelled], initial: requested }
      action create { requires self.assessment in [assessed, collected] }
      action apply {
        from: requested, to: applied, actor: { party: fines_to }, input { reason: text, evidence: text }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.assessment, action: waive, input: { reason: { field: input.reason }, evidence: { field: input.evidence } } }]
      }
      action cancel { from: requested, to: cancelled }
    }
    waiver: {
      fields { assessment: ref<parent>, amendment: ref<on.amendment>, amount: money }
      lifecycle { states: [recorded], initial: recorded }
      action create {
        actor: { parent: parent }, input { assessment: ref<parent>, amendment: ref<on.amendment>, amount: money }
        requires unique "amendment_waiver" on [self.assessment, self.amendment]
      }
    }
    receipt: {
      fields { cashReceipt: text?, plan: ref<on>, assessment: ref<parent>, payment: ref<on.payment>, amount: money }
      lifecycle { states: [paid, refunded], initial: paid }
      action create { actor: { parent: parent }, input { plan: ref<on>, assessment: ref<parent>, payment: ref<on.payment>, amount: money }, requires input.payment.plan == self.assessment.plan; requires unique "fine_receipt" on [self.assessment, self.payment]; moves self.amount from self.payment.held to fines_to capture "cashReceipt" economics { recipient: fines_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: borrower }, participant: { purpose: pass_through, sourceParty: programOperator } }; moves self.amount from self.plan.fineReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator } }
      action refund {
        from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: [parent, child(on, payment)] }
        moves self.amount from fines_to to self.payment.plan.borrower economics { recipient: fines_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: fines_to, reversalOf: self.cashReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
        moves self.amount from self.plan.debt to self.plan.fineReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.assessment, action: reopen, input: { amount: { field: self.amount } } }]
      }
      // unwind_paid returns the cash; the plan cancels the claims itself.
      action unwind { from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: on }, moves self.amount from fines_to to self.payment.plan.borrower economics { recipient: fines_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: fines_to, reversalOf: self.cashReceipt }, participant: unclassified } }
    }

    cost: {
      revisioned: true
      fields {
        plan: ref<on>, assessment: ref<parent>, overdueAt: date?, evidence: text, evidencedCost: money, amount: money = minimum(self.evidencedCost, cap), payoffAmount: money?, payoffReceipt: text?, payoffLed: integer?
        open: money?, take: money?
      }
      lifecycle { states: [proposed, assessed, collected, waived], initial: proposed }
      action create { actor: { party: programOperator }, calculate: [{ target: overdueAt, op: shift, date: { field: self.assessment.overdueAt }, milliseconds: { literal: 0 }, direction: after }, { target: payoffAmount, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }, { target: open, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }], requires unique "recovery_assessment" on [self.assessment]; requires self.plan == self.assessment.plan; requires count of { instrument: all(financing.late_charge.cost), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [proposed, assessed, collected], limit: 366 } < self.plan.historyLimit }
      action assess { allowZero: true,
        from: proposed, to: assessed, actor: clock, due: { at: self.assessment.overdueAt }
        requires self.assessment.slice.openPrincipal > "0"
        calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.amount }] }]
        moves self.amount from self.plan.debt to self.plan.costReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
      }
      action collect {
        from: [assessed, collected], to: assessed, actor: { parent: child(on, payment) }, input { payment: ref<on.payment> }
        requires input.payment in [paid]
        requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
        calculate: [{ target: take, op: minimum, values: [{ field: input.payment.held.balance }, { field: self.open }] }]
        invoke: [{ instrument: receipt, action: create, guard: { kind: compare, left: { field: self.take }, operator: ">", right: { literal: "0" } }, input: { plan: { field: self.plan }, assessment: { field: self.id }, payment: { field: input.payment }, amount: { field: self.take } } }, { reference: self.id, action: reduce, input: {} }, { selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: 1, where: { id: { field: self.id }, open: { literal: "0" } } }, action: finish, input: {} }]
      }
      action payoff { allowZero: true,
        from: assessed, to: collected, actor: { parent: on }
        requires self.plan in [paid]
        calculate: [{ target: payoffAmount, op: aggregate, selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: 366 }, measure: { sum: "open" } }]
        set: { payoffLed: { literal: 1 } }
        moves self.payoffAmount from self.plan.borrower to costs_to capture "payoffReceipt" economics { recipient: costs_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: borrower }, participant: { purpose: pass_through, sourceParty: borrower } }
        moves self.payoffAmount from self.plan.costReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: current(), reference: "plan", anchor: self.plan, states: [assessed], limit: 366 }, action: close, input: {} }, { reference: self.id, action: close, input: {} }]
      }
      action close { from: [assessed, collected], to: collected, actor: { parent: current() }, calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }] }
      action unwind_payoff { allowZero: true,
        from: collected, to: collected, actor: { parent: on }
        set: { payoffLed: { literal: 2 } }
        moves self.payoffAmount from costs_to to self.plan.borrower economics { recipient: costs_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: costs_to, reversalOf: self.payoffReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
      }
      action finish { from: assessed, to: collected, actor: { parent: current() }, requires self.open == "0" }
      action reduce { from: [assessed, collected, waived], to: preserve, actor: { parent: current() }, calculate: [{ target: open, op: subtract, base: { field: self.open }, subtract: [{ field: self.take }] }] }
      action cancel { from: proposed, to: waived, actor: { party: programOperator } }
      action cancel_for_amendment { from: proposed, to: waived, actor: { parent: child(on, amendment) } }
      action cancel_undelivered { from: [proposed, assessed, collected], to: waived, actor: { parent: on }, calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ literal: "0" }] }] }
      action waive_for_amendment {
        from: [assessed, collected], to: assessed, actor: { parent: child(on, amendment) }, input { amendment: ref<on.amendment> }
        requires input.amendment.plan == self.plan; requires input.amendment in [applied]
        calculate: [{ target: take, op: rate, base: { field: self.open }, bps: { field: input.amendment.waiverPercent }, rounding: floor }]
        invoke: [{ instrument: waiver, action: create, input: { assessment: { field: self.id }, amendment: { field: input.amendment }, amount: { field: self.take } } }, { reference: self.id, action: reduce, input: {} }]
      }
      action waive { allowZero: true,
        from: [assessed, collected], to: waived, actor: { parent: waiver_request }, input { reason: text, evidence: text }
        calculate: [{ target: take, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.open }] }]
        moves self.take from self.plan.costReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator }
        invoke: [{ reference: self.id, action: reduce, input: {} }]
      }
      action refund {
        from: [assessed, collected], to: preserve, actor: { party: costs_to }, input { payment: ref<on.payment> }, deadline: { at: self.plan.refundUntil }
        requires input.payment in [paid, refunded]
        requires input.payment.plan == self.plan
        invoke: [{ selection: { instrument: receipt, reference: "payment", anchor: input.payment, states: [paid], limit: 1, where: { assessment: { field: self.id } } }, action: refund, input: {} }]
      }
      action reopen {
        from: [assessed, collected], to: assessed, actor: { parent: receipt }, input { amount: money }
        calculate: [{ target: open, op: sum, values: [{ field: self.open }, { field: input.amount }] }]
      }
      records {
        waiver_request: {
          fields { assessment: ref<parent>, reason: text, evidence: text }
          lifecycle { states: [requested, applied, cancelled], initial: requested }
          action create { requires self.assessment in [assessed, collected] }
          action apply {
            from: requested, to: applied, actor: { party: costs_to }, input { reason: text, evidence: text }
            invoke: [{ reference: self.assessment, action: waive, input: { reason: { field: input.reason }, evidence: { field: input.evidence } } }]
          }
          action cancel { from: requested, to: cancelled }
        }
        waiver: {
          fields { assessment: ref<parent>, amendment: ref<on.amendment>, amount: money }
          lifecycle { states: [recorded], initial: recorded }
          action create {
            actor: { parent: parent }, input { assessment: ref<parent>, amendment: ref<on.amendment>, amount: money }
            requires unique "amendment_waiver" on [self.assessment, self.amendment]
          }
        }
        receipt: {
          fields { cashReceipt: text?, plan: ref<on>, assessment: ref<parent>, payment: ref<on.payment>, amount: money }
          lifecycle { states: [paid, refunded], initial: paid }
          action create { actor: { parent: parent }, input { plan: ref<on>, assessment: ref<parent>, payment: ref<on.payment>, amount: money }, requires input.payment.plan == self.assessment.plan; requires unique "cost_receipt" on [self.assessment, self.payment]; moves self.amount from self.payment.held to costs_to capture "cashReceipt" economics { recipient: costs_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: borrower }, participant: { purpose: pass_through, sourceParty: programOperator } }; moves self.amount from self.plan.costReceivable to self.plan.debt economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: programOperator } }
          action refund {
            from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: [parent, child(on, payment)] }
            moves self.amount from costs_to to self.payment.plan.borrower economics { recipient: costs_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: costs_to, reversalOf: self.cashReceipt }, participant: unclassified }
            moves self.amount from self.plan.debt to self.plan.costReceivable economics { purpose: internal, sourceParty: borrower }
            invoke: [{ reference: self.assessment, action: reopen, input: { amount: { field: self.amount } } }]
          }
          action unwind { from: paid, to: refunded, actor: { parent: on }, moves self.amount from costs_to to self.payment.plan.borrower economics { recipient: costs_to, company: { purpose: earning, sourceParty: costs_to, reversalOf: self.cashReceipt }, participant: unclassified } }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

instrument limits(per_borrower: money, borrower: party = party(person), active_plans: integer = 1) {
  familyRevision: 1
  scope: product
  summary: "One outstanding balance ceiling per borrower."
  fields { borrower: account of borrower, limit: money = per_borrower, activePlans: integer = active_plans }
  lifecycle { states: [pending, approved], initial: pending }
  action create { actor: { party: borrower }, requires unique "borrower_limit" on [self.borrower] }
  action approve { from: pending, to: approved, actor: { party: programOperator } }
}

instrument portfolio_limit(limit: money) {
  familyRevision: 1
  scope: product
  summary: "One shared ceiling on the principal the product may hold."
  fields { key: text = "portfolio", limit: money = limit }
  lifecycle { states: [pending, approved], initial: pending }
  action create { actor: { party: programOperator }, requires unique "portfolio_limit" on [self.key] }
  action approve { from: pending, to: approved, actor: { party: programOperator } }
}

instrument credit_line(borrower: party = programOperator, adapter: text, limit: money, expires: date) {
  familyRevision: 1
  summary: "A revolving facility from an outside lender; each draw is a separate immutable advance."
  fields { borrower: account of borrower, facility: account(borrower, cash, "facility"), debt: account(borrower, claim, contra, "debt"), limit: money = limit, expiresAt: date = expires }
  lifecycle { states: [pending, active, suspended, closed], initial: pending }
  action create { actor: { party: borrower } }
  action activate {
    from: pending, to: active, actor: { party: borrower }
    subject { adapter: adapter }
  }
  action suspend { from: active, to: suspended, actor: { party: borrower } }
  action resume { from: suspended, to: active, actor: { party: borrower } }
  action close { from: [active, suspended], to: closed, actor: { party: borrower }, due: { at: self.expiresAt }, requires count of { instrument: all(financing.advance), reference: "line", anchor: self.id, states: [drawn], limit: 366 } == 0 }
}

instrument advance(line: ref<financing.credit_line>, amount: money = runtime, borrower: party = programOperator) {
  familyRevision: 1
  summary: "A single facility draw with an immutable principal and full repayment."
  fields { line: ref<line>, borrower: account of borrower, amount: money = amount, principalReceivable: account(self, claim) }
  lifecycle { states: [pending, drawn, repaid, cancelled], initial: pending }
  action create { actor: { party: borrower }, requires self.borrower == self.line.borrower; requires self.amount <= self.line.limit }
  invariants sum "principalReceivable.balance" of { instrument: all(financing.advance), reference: "line", anchor: self.line, states: [drawn], limit: 366 } <= self.line.limit
  action draw {
    from: pending, to: drawn, actor: { party: borrower }
    requires self.line in [active]
    deadline: { at: self.line.expiresAt }
    moves self.amount from self.line.facility to self.line.borrower; moves self.amount from self.line.debt to self.principalReceivable
  }
  action repay { from: drawn, to: repaid, actor: { party: borrower }, moves self.amount from self.line.borrower to self.line.facility; moves self.amount from self.principalReceivable to self.line.debt }
  action cancel { from: pending, to: cancelled, actor: { party: borrower } }
}
